--- !u!114 &899607282
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 899607280}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b1b1198fa5b13d047b3edb9610bc8681, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::InteractableTarget
  targetTitle: Emperor Seamounts
  subTitle: 
  descriptionParagraphs:
  - "Geological Formation and OriginThe chain was formed by a stationary plume of
    magma rising from the Earth's mantle, known as the Hawaiian hotspot. As the Pacific
    Plate drifted over this stationary hotspot, magma erupted through the crust,
    forming islands that later eroded and submerged into seamounts (underwater mountains)
    and guyots (flat-topped seamounts). Due to plate movement, the age of the seamounts
    increases progressively toward the northwest. The youngest active volcano (L\u014D\u02BBihi
    Seamount) is at the southeastern end, while the oldest (Meiji Seamount) is at
    the northernmost end, dated at approximately 82 million years old. The Famous
    60-Degree BendOne of the most striking features of this chain is a sharp 60-degree
    bend that separates the younger Hawaiian Ridge from the older Emperor Seamounts.
    This bend occurred approximately 47 million years ago. For decades, scientists
    believed this represented a sudden change in the direction of the Pacific Plate's
    movement. However, recent studies suggest it may also have been caused by the
    hotspot itself drifting southward during its early history."
  displayImages:
  - {fileID: 21300000, guid: 551e3feb0786eb44ebd5e3ca2514bdcd, type: 3}
